@@s162 <a href="basi-firma.html">Signature</a>
@@s163 Operators that are methods
@@s164 In Scala also <code>+</code> and <code>::</code> are methods. Two rules are enough to read them.
@@s165 Who owns the method?
@@s166 A method with one argument can be written in the middle, without dot and brackets. The method belongs to the value on the <b>left</b>.
@@s167 It holds for any one-argument method, not only for symbols.
@@s168 Exception: if the operator <b>ends with a colon</b>, the method belongs to the value on the <b>right</b>.
@@s169 For the same reason several <code>::</code> in a row are computed from the right: first <code>3 :: Nil</code>.
@@s170 1 :: xs in memory: a new cell, the shared tail
